A||N||5||Eriamjh||Are my Front calipers toast?||||1||
Z||000000||Eriamjh||11-23-2001||07:58 PM||||'87 Fiero, Blue (woo hoo).<P>Ok, experts, my '87 has 40K on the front rotors and they too almost nothing off them to turn 'em.  They still measure close or original spec.<P>I suspect that both my front calipers are siezed, but get this: One of the two pads (the outboard one) was still worn to nothing while the inside pad was barely touched.<P>Is this a bad caliper or just poorly lubricating sliding pins?  <P>The car has always braked poorly, but I never thought I was driving around with no fronts at all.<P>What's the consensus? Thanks for all your help!||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||11-23-2001||08:43 PM||||Yep!! They have had it, put full rebuilt units on.  There's no point in going through all the work just to replace the sliders, might as well get new piston and seal boots at the same time, not much price difference. <P>Make sure you use a drop of "lock tite" on the caliper retaining bolts (ask parts supplier for the correct type to use, don't use permanent!).<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-23-2001||11:11 PM||||read my cave article for places to grease besides pins.... make sure you use Brake grease and not anything that's oil based!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||11-24-2001||11:06 AM||||Hey Dan!<BR>When you get calipers, get the "loaded" ones...<BR>They come with everything, including pads...<BR>Also replace your hoses!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-24-2001||01:32 PM||||Yes, at this point the factory hoses should probably be replaced on all Fiero that haven't already had at least one new set in their life. I prefer OE style hoses but that's up to you.<P>If you are keeping the lines and If you use penetrating oil, Make sure no oil gets on the rubber lines. It can ruin them very easily.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eriamjh||11-24-2001||04:17 PM||||New lines ordered from Fiero Store.<P>New calipers bought IN STOCK at Glendale Auto in Farmington Hills, MI for, get this: $25 each after core charge return and sales tax!  I checked the old ones.  They were stuck worse than Congress on   Health Insurance reform!!  Almost broke my caliper piston pushing-in tool!<P>I got both lines disconnected at the car without braking them.  What the hell kind of flare is that?  ||||reg||10
